1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:05,500
This is a job cost export out of the ERP.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:09,600
Three hundred and eighty lines. Every month.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,200
You need the list of vendors we actually bought from.

4
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:16,000
Copy the column, new tab, Remove Duplicates, sort — then do it again next month.

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,400
Here's the version that never needs doing twice.

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:23,000
One formula: UNIQUE — and the vendor column.

7
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:27,400
Excel writes the table reference for you.

8
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:33,400
Fifteen vendors, out of three hundred and eighty lines.

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:38,900
I never told it fifteen. It took exactly the space it needed.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,900
Every cell in that list belongs to the one formula in B5.

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,700
That's a spill range.

12
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:52,000
It isn't sorted — so wrap the whole thing in SORT.

13
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:56,400
One more function around the outside. Nothing else changes.

14
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:01,000
Alphabetical. Still one formula.

15
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:04,200
Now the useful one.

16
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:10,500
FILTER — give it the whole table...

17
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:18,400
...then the rule: cost center equals this cell.

18
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:25,000
A hundred and thirty-six lines. Every one charged to Powder Line 1.

19
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:28,400
And here's the part that matters.

20
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:33,000
Change the cost center...

21
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:39,000
...and the whole report redraws itself.

22
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:43,000
No copying. No pasting. No re-sorting.
